<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
  <title>Dashboard | Scott's Armchair &amp; Knitting Service</title>
  <meta name="robots" content="noindex, nofollow">
  <%- include('partials/styles') %>
</head>
<body class="scott-body">
  <div class="sc-shell">
    <%- include('partials/sidebar', { active: 'dashboard' }) %>
    <main class="sc-main">
      <% if (typeof isImpersonating !== 'undefined' && isImpersonating) { %>
        <div class="sc-impersonation-banner">Demonstration mode: viewing as <%= persona.name %>, Clearance <%= persona.code %> (<%= persona.role %>). This is exactly what they can see.</div>
      <% } %>
      <%
        // The front door, staged. Ruth is the centrepiece, the
        // specialists are arrayed beneath her so 'one receptionist, many
        // workers' reads at a glance, and the routing lights up live as
        // she hands work over. Presentation only: same widget, same API,
        // same clearance, same everything underneath.
      %>
      <section class="sc-stage">
        <div class="sc-stage-topbar">
          <span class="sc-stage-kicker">A fictional company run by a governed AI team &middot; a working demonstration by Arrington Consultancy</span>
          <% if (!canImpersonate) { %>
            <span class="sc-stage-viewer-fixed"><%= persona.name %> &middot; <%= persona.role %> &middot; Clearance <%= persona.code %></span>
          <% } %>
        </div>

        <% if (canImpersonate) { %>
        <div class="sc-persona-chips-wrap">
          <div class="sc-persona-chips-label">Switch viewpoint</div>
          <div class="sc-persona-chips-row">
            <%
              var activePersonaId = (typeof isImpersonating !== 'undefined' && isImpersonating) ? personaId : '';
            %>
            <button class="sc-persona-chip sc-persona-chip-owner<%= activePersonaId === '' ? ' active' : '' %>" data-persona-id="">
              <div class="sc-persona-chip-dot">SM</div>
              <div>
                <div class="sc-persona-chip-name">Scott Mercer</div>
                <div class="sc-persona-chip-role">Owner &middot; <span class="sc-persona-chip-code">07Q</span></div>
              </div>
            </button>
            <% Object.keys(personas).forEach(function (id) { var p = personas[id]; %>
            <button class="sc-persona-chip<%= activePersonaId === id ? ' active' : '' %>" data-persona-id="<%= id %>">
              <div class="sc-persona-chip-dot"><%= p.code.substring(0,2) %></div>
              <div>
                <div class="sc-persona-chip-name"><%= p.name %></div>
                <div class="sc-persona-chip-role"><%= p.role %> &middot; <span class="sc-persona-chip-code"><%= p.code %></span></div>
              </div>
            </button>
            <% }); %>
          </div>
        </div>
        <% } %>

        <div class="sc-stage-ruth">
          <div class="sc-stage-avatar"><span><%= ruth.initials %></span></div>
          <div class="sc-stage-ruth-id">
            <div class="sc-stage-ruth-name"><%= ruth.characterName %></div>
            <div class="sc-stage-ruth-role"><%= ruth.displayRole %> &middot; <%= ruth.tagline %></div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <h1 class="sc-stage-h">What do you need help with?</h1>

        <div class="sc-stage-chat">
          <%- include('partials/chat-widget', { workersById: workersById, csrfToken: csrfToken, aiEnabled: aiEnabled, heroFocus: true, heroMode: true }) %>
        </div>

        <div class="sc-suggestions-wrap">
          <div class="sc-suggestions-label">Ask Ruth</div>
          <div class="sc-suggestions-row">
            <%
              var _personaSuggestions = {
                scott_mercer: [
                  "Where are we losing money we're not tracking?",
                  "Which jobs are at risk this week?",
                  "Show me the commercial leakage opportunities",
                  "Is there anything that needs my approval today?",
                  "What does Tony see that the team doesn't?"
                ],
                tony_marsh: [
                  "What jobs are at risk of missing their promised date?",
                  "Is capacity tight this week?",
                  "Which customers have overdue returns?",
                  "What stock issues could slow us down?",
                  "Are there any jobs waiting on materials?"
                ],
                chloe_reed: [
                  "Which enquiries are waiting on a quote?",
                  "Do we have any overdue invoices?",
                  "What's in the active pipeline this week?",
                  "Are there any complaints that need a follow-up?",
                  "Which customers haven't heard from us recently?"
                ],
                leah_morgan: [
                  "What's my first knitting job this morning?",
                  "Have my new knitting needles arrived yet?",
                  "What's the wool supply like for this week?",
                  "Are any of my jobs running late?",
                  "What yarn do I need for the jobs on the board?"
                ],
                ellie_park: [
                  "What are my jobs for today?",
                  "Are there any jobs waiting on materials?",
                  "Which repairs are due to go out this week?",
                  "Is there anything blocked on the workshop floor?",
                  "What's next in the repair queue?"
                ],
                ravi_singh: [
                  "What are my assigned jobs today?",
                  "Are there any quality checks I need to complete?",
                  "What jobs are waiting on my attention?",
                  "Is there anything I need to flag before I start?",
                  "Which jobs are due out this week?"
                ],
                jo_bell: [
                  "What knitting work is assigned to me today?",
                  "Is the yarn I need in stock?",
                  "Are any of my jobs running behind?",
                  "What's next on my list after the current job?",
                  "Have we had any new knitting jobs come in?"
                ],
                mike_evans: [
                  "What am I driving today?",
                  "Where is my first delivery today?",
                  "Are there any collections I need to pick up on my route?",
                  "Is the van ready to go?",
                  "Has anything changed on today's schedule?"
                ]
              };
              var _chips = _personaSuggestions[personaId] || _personaSuggestions['scott_mercer'];
              _chips.forEach(function (chip) {
            %>
            <button class="sc-suggestion-chip"><%- chip %></button>
            <% }); %>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="sc-team-strip" aria-label="The specialists Ruth routes to">
          <div class="sc-team-lead-in">Ruth routes your question to</div>
          <div class="sc-team-row">
            <% specialists.forEach(function (w) { %>
              <div class="sc-team-chip" data-team-worker="<%= w.id %>">
                <div class="sc-team-avatar sc-avatar-<%= w.id %>"><%= w.initials %></div>
                <div class="sc-team-meta">
                  <div class="sc-team-name"><%= w.characterName %></div>
                  <div class="sc-team-role"><%= w.displayRole %></div>
                </div>
              </div>
            <% }); %>
          </div>
          <div class="sc-stage-footnote">What you can see, and what the team will agree to do, depends on who is signed in. <a href="/scott/team">How this team works</a>.</div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <script nonce="<%= nonce %>">
      // Live routing lights. The chat widget calls window.scTeamPing as
      // Ruth thinks and each specialist starts and finishes answering;
      // this just moves the glow around the stage. Presentation only.
      window.scTeamPing = (function () {
        var stage = document.querySelector('.sc-stage');
        function chip(id) { return document.querySelector('.sc-team-chip[data-team-worker="' + id + '"]'); }
        return function (workerId, state) {
          if (!stage) return;
          if (state === 'idle') {
            stage.classList.remove('sc-stage-thinking');
            return;
          }
          if (workerId === 'receptionist') {
            if (state === 'thinking') stage.classList.add('sc-stage-thinking');
            return;
          }
          var c = chip(workerId);
          if (!c) return;
          if (state === 'thinking') {
            c.classList.add('is-routing');
          } else if (state === 'answered') {
            c.classList.remove('is-routing');
            c.classList.add('is-answered');
            setTimeout(function () { c.classList.remove('is-answered'); }, 2600);
          }
        };
      })();
      </script>

      <%
        // The pulse: the four numbers an owner actually glances at, big
        // and unboxed. The overdue-money figure is clearance-gated like
        // everything else; below debtor clearance the fourth number is
        // the week's due jobs instead.
        var pulseMoney = null;
        if (canSee('debtor_flag')) {
          pulseMoney = (facts.CUSTOMERS || []).reduce(function (t, c) { return t + (c.overdueGbp || 0); }, 0);
        }
      %>
      <section class="sc-pulse">
        <a class="sc-pulse-item" href="/scott/jobs?at_risk=1">
          <span class="sc-pulse-num <%= summary.atRiskJobs ? 'warn' : '' %>"><%= summary.atRiskJobs %></span>
          <span class="sc-pulse-label">Jobs at risk</span>
        </a>
        <a class="sc-pulse-item" href="/scott/approvals">
          <span class="sc-pulse-num <%= summary.pendingApprovals ? 'warn' : '' %>"><%= summary.pendingApprovals %></span>
          <span class="sc-pulse-label">Awaiting your approval</span>
        </a>
        <a class="sc-pulse-item" href="/scott/enquiries?status=new">
          <span class="sc-pulse-num"><%= summary.newEnquiries %></span>
          <span class="sc-pulse-label">New enquiries</span>
        </a>
        <% if (pulseMoney !== null) { %>
        <a class="sc-pulse-item" href="/scott/customers">
          <span class="sc-pulse-num <%= pulseMoney ? 'warn' : '' %>">&pound;<%= pulseMoney.toLocaleString() %></span>
          <span class="sc-pulse-label">Overdue money</span>
        </a>
        <% } else { %>
        <a class="sc-pulse-item" href="/scott/jobs">
          <span class="sc-pulse-num"><%= summary.dueThisWeek %></span>
          <span class="sc-pulse-label">Due within 7 days</span>
        </a>
        <% } %>
      </section>
      <p class="sc-pulse-sub"><%= summary.openJobs %> open jobs &middot; <%= summary.dueThisWeek %> due within 7 days &middot; <a href="/scott/jobs">Jobs &amp; Orders</a></p>

      <%
        // The switch handler for #scPersonaSelect lives in the sidebar
        // partial (included on every page), which binds it wherever the
        // select exists. No second script here, or the change event would
        // fire twice.
      %>


      <%
        // Open material gaps, above the attention list on purpose: a
        // record that is wrong makes everything below it unreliable, and
        // 07H's own rule says the dashboard is a summary layer rather
        // than the highest source of truth. Already clearance-filtered
        // server-side, so this loop does no gating of its own.
      %>
      <% if (openGaps.length) { %>
        <h2 class="sc-section-title">Needs human input</h2>
        <div class="sc-card sc-honesty-card">
          <p class="sc-row-sub"><strong><%= openGaps.length %> open <%= openGaps.length === 1 ? 'gap' : 'gaps' %> in the records</strong><% if (myGaps.length) { %>, <%= myGaps.length %> waiting on you<% } %>. These are not approvals. Something in a controlled record is missing, out of date or contradictory, and nothing downstream of it can be relied on until a person corrects the source.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="sc-list">
          <% openGaps.slice(0, 5).forEach(function (g) { %>
            <div class="sc-card sc-row-card<%= g.work_can_continue ? '' : ' sc-gap-blocking' %>">
              <div>
                <div class="sc-row-sub">
                  <strong><%= g.missing_evidence %></strong><br>
                  <%= g.why_it_matters %><br>
                  <strong>Correct or confirm:</strong> <%= g.expected_source || g.domain %>
                  &middot; <strong>Responsible:</strong> <%= g.responsible_name || 'nobody recorded yet' %><br>
                  <%= describeNotification(g) %>
                </div>
              </div>
              <div class="sc-row-actions">
                <% if (!g.work_can_continue) { %><span class="sc-pill sc-pill-risk">work stopped</span><% } %>
                <span class="sc-pill sc-pill-status"><%= g.gap_type %></span>
              </div>
            </div>
          <% }); %>
        </div>
        <p class="sc-proposed-note"><a href="/scott/gaps">Open the full register</a>. A gap only closes when a person has corrected or confirmed the source, never by an AI worker deciding it no longer matters.</p>
      <% } %>

      <h2 class="sc-section-title">What needs your attention today</h2>
      <% var mine = facts.ATTENTION_TODAY.filter(function (a) { return canSee(a.domain); }); %>
      <% if (!mine.length) { %>
        <div class="sc-card sc-empty">
          Nothing on the management attention list is yours today. That is not an empty company: it is a
          list of decisions above your clearance, and none of them are waiting on you. Your own work is
          under Jobs &amp; Orders.
        </div>
      <% } else { %>
        <div class="sc-list">
          <% mine.forEach(function (a) { %>
            <div class="sc-card sc-row-card">
              <div>
                <div class="sc-row-sub"><%= a.item %><% if (a.action) { %><br><strong>What to do:</strong> <%= a.action %><% } %></div>
              </div>
              <div class="sc-row-actions"><span class="sc-pill sc-pill-status"><%= a.domain.replace(/_/g, ' ') %></span></div>
            </div>
          <% }); %>
        </div>
        <p class="sc-proposed-note"><%= facts.DASHBOARD_SOURCE_RULE.rule %></p>
      <% } %>

      <div class="sc-detail-grid">
        <div>
          <h2 class="sc-section-title">Recent activity</h2>
          <div class="sc-card sc-activity-card">
            <% if (!activity.length) { %>
              <div class="sc-empty">Nothing recorded yet. Ask Ruth a question to get started.</div>
            <% } else { %>
              <ul class="sc-activity-list">
                <% activity.forEach(function (a) { %>
                  <li class="sc-activity-item">
                    <span class="sc-activity-dot sc-dot-<%= workersById[a.actor] ? a.actor : (a.actor === 'user' ? 'user' : 'system') %>"></span>
                    <div>
                      <div><%= a.summary %></div>
                      <div class="sc-activity-meta">
                        <%= (workersById[a.actor] && workersById[a.actor].characterName) || a.actor %>
                        <% if (a.related_job_ref) { %> &middot; <a href="/scott/jobs/<%= a.related_job_ref %>"><%= a.related_job_ref %></a><% } %>
                        &middot; <%= new Date(a.created_at).toLocaleDateString('en-GB', { day: 'numeric', month: 'short' }) %>
                      </div>
                    </div>
                  </li>
                <% }); %>
              </ul>
            <% } %>
          </div>

        </div>
        <div>
          <h2 class="sc-section-title">Business snapshot</h2>
          <p class="sc-snapshot-label"><%= snapshotLabel %></p>
          <div class="sc-snapshot-stack">
            <% snapshotCards.forEach(function (c) { %>
              <div class="sc-card sc-stat">
                <div class="sc-stat-label"><%= c.label %></div>
                <div class="sc-stat-value sc-stat-value-sm"><%= c.value %></div>
                <div class="sc-stat-sub"><%= c.detail %></div>
              </div>
            <% }); %>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </main>
  </div>

  <!-- First-session welcome overlay (sessionStorage-gated, hidden once dismissed) -->
  <div class="sc-welcome-overlay" id="scWelcomeOverlay" hidden>
    <div class="sc-welcome-card">
      <div class="sc-welcome-head">
        <div class="sc-brand-mark">SA</div>
        <h2>Welcome to Scott&rsquo;s Armchair &amp; Knitting Service</h2>
        <p>A live demonstration of a real AI workforce in a fictional company. Nine workers, each with their own name, speciality and clearance level, run this business. You are the operator.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="sc-welcome-body">
        <div class="sc-welcome-steps">
          <div class="sc-welcome-step"><span class="sc-welcome-step-num">1</span><div><strong>Ask Ruth a question</strong><br>Type anything in the chat. Ruth reads your question, decides which specialist to consult, and gives you a governed answer.</div></div>
          <div class="sc-welcome-step"><span class="sc-welcome-step-num">2</span><div><strong>Switch viewpoint</strong><br>Use the persona chips above the chat to see the system through different eyes. Tony sees less than Scott. Mike sees less than Tony. Every permission boundary is real.</div></div>
          <div class="sc-welcome-step"><span class="sc-welcome-step-num">3</span><div><strong>Explore the records</strong><br>Use the left-hand menu to open any area. The same clearance rules apply everywhere: the same question, the same data, different answers depending on who is signed in.</div></div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="sc-welcome-foot">
        <button class="sc-btn sc-btn-primary sc-welcome-dismiss" id="scWelcomeDismiss">Start exploring</button>
        <a href="/scott/team" class="sc-welcome-skip">How does the team work?</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <script nonce="<%= nonce %>">
  (function () {
    var overlay = document.getElementById('scWelcomeOverlay');
    var dismiss = document.getElementById('scWelcomeDismiss');
    if (!overlay) return;
    try {
      if (!sessionStorage.getItem('sc-welcome-seen')) {
        overlay.hidden = false;
      }
    } catch (e) {}
    if (dismiss) {
      dismiss.addEventListener('click', function () {
        overlay.hidden = true;
        try { sessionStorage.setItem('sc-welcome-seen', '1'); } catch (e) {}
      });
    }
    overlay.addEventListener('click', function (e) {
      if (e.target === overlay) {
        overlay.hidden = true;
        try { sessionStorage.setItem('sc-welcome-seen', '1'); } catch (e) {}
      }
    });
  })();

  // Suggestion chips — fill and submit the Ruth chat input
  document.querySelectorAll('.sc-suggestion-chip').forEach(function (chip) {
    chip.addEventListener('click', function () {
      var inp = document.getElementById('scChatInput');
      var form = inp && inp.closest('form');
      if (!inp) return;
      inp.value = chip.textContent.trim();
      if (form) form.dispatchEvent(new Event('submit', { bubbles: true, cancelable: true }));
    });
  });
  </script>
</body>
</html>
